    "result_text": "The change is complete and the build passes. Here's what I did.\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated the three separate duplicate checks (telephone, email, household) on `POST /api/owners` into a single derived **identity key**, and now expose that key on the owner response.\n\n**The identity key** \u2014 `<normalizedTelephone>|<email or empty>|<householdId or empty>` \u2014 lives in one place, as a derived `@Transient` getter on the `Owner` entity (`Owner.getIdentityKey()`), alongside the existing derived getters (`getLocality`, `getContactPreference`, `getInitials`). This is the single source of truth used both for the check and for the response.\n\n**The single check** \u2014 new `EnsureUniqueIdentity` function replaces `EnsureUniqueTelephone`, `EnsureUniqueEmail`, and `EnsureUniqueHousehold`. It compares the new owner's whole identity key against existing owners and rejects (409) only on an exact full-key match. Since telephone is the first key component, an existing owner can only collide if it shares the telephone, so it reuses the existing `findByTelephone` lookup as the candidate set rather than scanning everything.\n\n**Ordering** \u2014 the check runs *after* `AssignHousehold` (so the new owner carries its final `householdId`, part of the key) and *before* `SaveOwner`, under the same `transaction` governance, so a collision rolls back before anything persists. `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`/`NormalizeOwnerEmail` still run first, so the key is built from normalized values.\n\n**Behaviour change (per spec):** two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with different telephones now have different keys and are both allowed \u2014 only an exact full-key match is a duplicate.\n\n**Return** \u2014 added a read-only `identityKey` to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml`; MapStruct maps it onto `OwnerDto` automatically by name.\n\n**Cleanup** \u2014 deleted the three obsolete check functions, the three `Duplicate*Exception` classes + handlers, and their escalation YAMLs; added `DuplicateIdentityException` + handler (409, body `{\"errors\":[\"identityKey\"]}`) and its escalation YAML; updated the `Household` javadoc that referenced the removed class.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsIdentityCollision` passes, **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
